-- statement:
--   For the original rational field embedded in the fixed algebraic closure, the original prime generated by a rational prime has integer and rational valuations exactly equal to the original negative p-adic valuation exponential. The valuation on rational units has additive exponent equal to the negative ordinary rational p-adic valuation. The original field, integer-ring equivalence, prime ideal, and every prime and nonzero hypothesis are retained. Named downstream consumer: the original actual pi Selmer rational radicand prime-divisibility and thirteen-support theorem.

